sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2019-boundary-12> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The volume of possible cognitive light cones (spatio-temporal boundaries of agents' goals) has presumably kept expanding over evolutionary time, through innovations in body structure that drastically enlarge the cognitive boundary, although some lineages contract it permanently or in particular life stages.";
    dc:type "historical-inference";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Cognitive light cones have expanded over evolutionary time";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “The Computational Boundary of a \"Self\": Developmental Bioelectricity Drives Multicellularity and Scale-Free Cognition”, Frontiers in psychology (2019), doi:10.3389/fpsyg.2019.02688; section “Defining Individuation From a Cognitive Perspective”. Scope: Evolution of agents across the tree of life"
}
